<title>INDIA: India's ACC falls 4.2 percent on NSE.</title>
<headline>India's ACC falls 4.2 percent on NSE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of India's Associated Cement Companies (ACC) slid 82 rupees or 4.15 to 1,896 rupees on the National Stock Exchange (NSE) in afternoon trade on Monday, brokers said.</p>
<p>They said one foreign fund was a seller in the stock.  </p>
<p>Analysts said a series of cost increases including fuel, freight and power have led to escalating production costs at a time when signs of oversupply in the cement sector are evident in several regions.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
